MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Eagles and Neil Diamond feel like natural next choices because familiar classic rock and melodic older songs fit my listening to classic rock hits and Simon & Garfunkel.",
    "Frankie Valli & The 4 Seasons fits the nostalgic sixties mood of AM Gold, while Bread appeals to the gentle, melodic side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour does not fit my current preference for familiar older hits. Although 25 interests me, I would still choose a classic hits collection today.",
    "Number One Hits and The Greatest Hits Collection leave me unsure whose music I would be choosing; a hits title alone does not establish a match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in greatest-hits albums seems to have been treated as enough on its own, when the artist and songs are what make those collections appealing.",
    "My occasional interest in newer pop seems to carry more weight than it should for what I want right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The softer, melodic side of my older-music listening matters: Bread appeals more than Santana this time, even though both connect to my classic rock interests.",
    "Cheek to Cheek suggests some interest in vocal standards, but I would need to know the artist and songs before choosing To Be Loved on that basis."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly recognize my interest in nostalgic hits, but sometimes miss that familiar artists and a gentle melodic sound matter more than a hits label or a broad pop connection."
}
